From 03005ca808e31450de4dd2bfae4bc622e65950e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:10:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] expand: `$crate` inside a derive's AST input goes to the proc
 macro as `$crate`

ron 0.12.2 (skim 5.7.3) extensions.rs puts `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]`
on a `bitflags!` struct; bitflags 2.13.2 public.rs expands that to

    struct Extensions(<Extensions as $crate::__private::PublicFlags>::Internal);

so the derive's input holds a path whose crate is bitflags's real name
(`$crate` from a macro_rules body is `::"<crate>"`, parsed into an Absolute
path). The serialiser's visit_path only knew the two parser forms, `crate`
and `=name` (a 2018 `::name::` path), and asserted on the third:

    Assertion failed: (pe.crate.c_str()[0] == '='), function visit_path,
    file src/expand/proc_macro.cpp, line 1047.

0117 handled the same thing for token-tree input (`send_dollar_crate`: one
`$crate` ident out, `::"<crate>"` back in). Use it here too, so a derive on
a struct from another crate's macro sees `$crate` as rustc shows it, and
a field type the derive repeats (serde's Deserialize does) resolves to that
crate again. A `$crate` of the current crate is the same case (its real
name, resolved as the current crate by Resolve).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/expand/proc_macro.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/expand/proc_macro.cpp b/src/expand/proc_macro.cpp
index dab9af37..9d615eda 100644
--- a/src/expand/proc_macro.cpp
+++ b/src/expand/proc_macro.cpp
@@ -1041,12 +1041,19 @@ namespace {
                 if( pe.crate == "" ) {
                     m_pmi.send_rword("crate");
                 }
-                else {
+                else if( pe.crate.c_str()[0] == '=' ) {
+                    // 2018 `::cratename::` path (see the parser)
                     m_pmi.send_symbol("::");
-                    //m_pmi.send_string(pe.crate.c_str());
-                    assert(pe.crate.c_str()[0] == '=');
                     m_pmi.send_ident(pe.crate.c_str() + 1);
                 }
+                else {
+                    // A real crate name: `$crate` from a macro_rules expansion, parsed from `::"<crate>"` (see the
+                    // macro_rules evaluator). This is the AST counterpart of the token-tree case in `visit_tokentree`:
+                    // the proc macro gets one `$crate` ident, mapped back to this crate on the way out.
+                    // - ron 0.12.2 extensions.rs: `bitflags! { #[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)] pub struct Extensions .. }`
+                    //   (bitflags 2.13.2 public.rs: `struct $PublicBitFlags(<$PublicBitFlags as $crate::__private::PublicFlags>::Internal)`)
+                    m_pmi.send_dollar_crate(pe.crate.c_str());
+                }
                 m_pmi.send_symbol("::");
                 nodes = &pe.nodes;
                 }
